    "title": "pandas.errors.NumExprClobberingError — pandas 3.1.0.dev0 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.errors.NumExprClobberingError#\n\n- exception pandas.errors.NumExprClobberingError[source]#\n- Exception raised when trying to use a built-in numexpr name as a variable name. `eval` or`query` will throw the error if the engine is set\nto ‘numexpr’. ‘numexpr’ is the default engine value for these methods if the\nnumexpr package is installed.See also \n  - `eval`\n  - Evaluate a Python expression as a string using various backends.\n  - `DataFrame.query`\n  - Query the columns of a DataFrame with a boolean expression.\n Examples >>> df = pd.DataFrame({\"abs\": [1, 1, 1]}) >>> df.query(\"abs > 2\") ... # NumExprClobberingError: Variables in expression \"(abs) > (2)\" overlap... >>> sin, a = 1, 2 >>> pd.eval(\"sin + a\", engine=\"numexpr\") ... # NumExprClobberingError: Variables in expression \"(sin) + (a)\" overlap...",
